# ek-machinecreate: enter the 64DD CREATE MACHINE mode from the SELECT MODE grid.
#
# EXPANSION-KIT-ONLY, AND DISK-ONLY, for exactly the reasons ek-courseedit.gdxs gives:
# main_menu.c:222's EK arm bounces the cursor off MODE_COURSE_EDIT (4) and
# MODE_CREATE_MACHINE (7) whenever gLeoDriveConnectionState == 0. NOT a corpus replay,
# not in covdrift.sh's set, SHOTs hand-placed -- the thing being proved is that a screen
# exists and what it says, not that the schedule covers a census.
#
# Grid geometry (main_menu.c:612): index = (row * 4) + column, cursor starts at
# MODE_GP_RACE = 0 (game/common.c:21). MODE_CREATE_MACHINE = 7 = row 1, column 3, so the
# walk is DOWN (0 -> 4) then RIGHT three times (4 -> 5 -> 6 -> 7). A enters.
#
# B11m: this is the machine-creator half of the English text pack's receipt -- the three
# reshaped Create-Machine labels (aMachineCreateMachineNameTex, aMachineCreateSettingsTex,
# D_xk3_80138930) are the only pack rows whose GEOMETRY changes with the translation, and
# machine_create_draw.c:402/908 pick that geometry off gdx_ek_disk_is_translated().
build native/ektranslate
seed1 0x1234abcd
seed2 0x0fedcba9
pins renderthread=1 bridgemain=1 det=1
note SELECT MODE grid is 4x2; CREATE MACHINE is index 7 (row 1, column 3).
at 350
wait 1
at 400
press START 15 0
at 600
wait 1
shot menu_before
at 660
press DOWN 12 0
at 760
press RIGHT 12 0
at 860
press RIGHT 12 0
at 960
press RIGHT 12 0
at 1060
wait 1
shot menu_cursor
at 1120
press A 12 0
at 1300
wait 1
shot enter_0
at 1600
wait 1
shot enter_1
at 2000
wait 1
shot enter_2
at 2500
wait 1
shot enter_3
at 3000
wait 1
shot enter_4
at 3500
wait 1
shot enter_5
len 3600
